 - **C++ signature cleanup:** collapsed **safe multiline C++ function declarations/definitions** to one physical line across the DLL source, making **signatures easier to grep, compare, and review** in diffs/LLM-assisted passes. Done with the help of the new [`collapse_cpp_signatures.py`](/LLM_Helpers/README.md#collapse_cpp_signaturespy), a **conservative** signature-only helper, which intentionally skips ordinary multiline calls and unsafe comments, while also supporting traceable hoisting for reviewed whole-line comments inside signatures; review its output as a mechanical source-cleanup tool rather than a general C++ formatter. It was empirically idempotent after the first full DLL pass (rerunning reported no safe C++ signature collapses found). This is especially useful for **overloaded functions** like `void addMessage`, or e.g., `void CvDeal::endTrade(TradeData trade, PlayerTypes eFromPlayer, PlayerTypes eToPlayer, bool bTeam, /* advc.036: */ bool bUpdateAttitude, PlayerTypes eCancelPlayer) // advc.130p`, instead of its old three-line equivalent.
 - **C++ inline-return cleanup:** collapsed simple inline DLL header functions whose bodies were exactly one `return` statement to one physical line, making trivial getters/wrappers easier to grep and compare. Done with the help of [`collapse_cpp_inline_returns.py`](/LLM_Helpers/README.md#collapse_cpp_inline_returnspy), a conservative mechanical helper that skips constructors/destructors, multi-statement bodies, body comments, multiline signatures, and overlong results. For example, `int getGoldPerTurnByPlayer(PlayerTypes ePlayer) const { return m_aiGoldPerTurnByPlayer.get(ePlayer); } // Exposed to Python`, instead of its old four-line equivalent.
 - **Build cleanup - disabled unneeded DLL test code in normal builds:** compile-gated disabled reproducibility-test code (`ReproTest.cpp`) so normal DLL builds no longer compile it unless explicitly enabled for debugging. This keeps dormant test/debug code out of normal builds, may slightly reduce DLL/build size, and does **not** change gameplay. Found with the help of the new [`find_cpp_dead_code_candidates.py`](/LLM_Helpers/find_cpp_dead_code_candidates.py) LLM/manual-review helper.
-- **GitHub workflow build checks:** added GitHub Actions checks under [`.github/workflows`](/.github/workflows/) to catch forgotten debug/default settings and data drift at each commit. Current checks notably verify launch-guard sentinel values, XML tag references in SAS define text values, integer SAS define bounds, valid main-menu opening-music script setup, disabled BBAI logging defaults, shared UI font defaults, Sevopedia Leader AI Personality Panel predumped-cache defaults and predump file presence, `WorldSizeTypes` enum/XML alignment, `CvGameCoreDLL/Project/temp_files/` staying effectively empty (only its tracked placeholder file), not being ignored by `.gitignore`, and being allowed only as an archive-excluded development marker through `.gitattributes` (helps catch stale fast-compile temp files. We check this because we suspect fast compiles can be unreliable, and also helps catch forgetting to replace the committed DLL after compiling; see [KI#38](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#38---no-idea-why-but-sometimes-compile-mysteriouslystrangelyinconsistently-fails-and-recompiling-succeeds-underwith-but-exact-same-source-files-if-i-am-not-mistaken-but) and [KI#38.2](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#382---weird-dll-xml-errors-at-launch-solved-by-recompiling-the-exact-same-dll-cosmic-ray-2-or-something-else-maybe-or-whatever-maybe-but)), and every playable `PrivateMaps/*.py` being listed exactly once across the SAS map-script heaviness/coverage defines while every listed map script exists in `PrivateMaps/`. For example, this helped spot [map scripts that were previously unclassified in SAS map-script heaviness defines](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27198308080/job/80295526028); they are now listed explicitly for exhaustiveness (more robust; no gameplay change).
