 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6089+) **Update :** military-production logging exposed an AdvCiv-SAS-specific edge case where this defender-to-offense substitution could rewrite a `UNITAI_CITY_DEFENSE` request even when the caller had explicitly determined that a real city defender or Settler escort was required. In one pre-fix save-file 456 sample, 98 of 322 minimum-defender requests were converted to another UnitAI; concrete examples included Pasargadae requesting a Longbowman for minimum defense but receiving a Catapult with `UNITAI_ATTACK_CITY`, and Thebes repeatedly requesting defense for an existing Settler but likewise receiving offensive units. To fix this, the optimization now preserves concrete `UNITAI_CITY_DEFENSE` requests when the strict city-defender count is below `AI_minDefenders() + plot Settlers`, plus the existing thin-military post-Settler case. In the final save-file 456 run, all 264 minimum-defender choices, 34 existing-Settler escort choices, 8 zero-defender choices and 5 quick post-Settler defense choices kept their requested UnitAI, while 15 ordinary floating-defender requests were still redirected to offense. Save file 457 independently reproduced the separation: 262 minimum-defender completions, 24 Settler-escort defenses and 9 zero-defender branches had zero SAS role rewrites, while floating-defender production still made 65 ordinary substitutions. See [KI#197.4](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#1974---fixedimproved-advciv-sas-excess-defender-optimization-could-replace-explicitly-required-unitai_city_defense-production-with-offensive-unitais-including-minimum-defenders-and-settler-escorts).
